.TH HYPERCUBE 1
.SH NAME
hypercube \- tumbling tesseract, a 4-dimensional wireframe demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/hypercube
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Hypercube
is a work-alike of the "Mind's Eye more: n dimensions" chapter of
Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
a 16-vertex 4-dimensional hypercube, rotating simultaneously in two
4-D planes (a single plane alone looks like an ordinary 3-D spin; two
together is what actually reads as tumbling in 4 dimensions).
.PP
Each vertex is perspective-divided down to ordinary 3-D by its own
distance along the fourth axis, then drawn with the usual
.IR draw3d (2)
wireframe pipeline. Each of the four axes (x/y/z/w) is drawn in its
own colour (red/green/blue/yellow), the standard convention for
reading a 4-D wireframe.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/hypercube.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw3ddemo (1)
